<article class="env-lemma" id="0DHU">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0DHU">Lemma <span data-tag="0DHU">15.85.3</span>.</a> Let $R \to A$ be a flat ring map of finite presentation. A perfect object of $D(A)$ is $R$-perfect. If $K, M \in D(A)$ then $K \otimes _ A^\mathbf {L} M$ is $R$-perfect if $K$ is perfect and $M$ is $R$-perfect. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      The first statement follows from the second by taking $M = A$. The second statement follows from Lemmas <a href="/tag/0658" data-tag="0658">15.76.2</a>, <a href="/tag/0B66" data-tag="0B66">15.68.10</a>, and <a href="/tag/0DJE" data-tag="0DJE">15.66.16</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>